WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.870
(One month until the Winter
 International Sports GP at Sapporo)

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.230
Expectations for medals are highest
 with the 200m ski jump.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.040
It will take place at
 Forest of Light Hill.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.620
Its premiere is in two days,
 on January 6.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.990
(Three Birdmen)

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.410
The Three Birdmen, representing Japan,
 will do an exhibition jump.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.370
(January 3rd,
 the 47th of Shinka Era, Sapporo)

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.910
Great, Mr. Amato.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.540
Zenda.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.580
I mean, Birdman Shin, was it?

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:45.000
Come on. Just call me Zenda.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:46.620
I couldn't.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.250
You guys represent Japan.
 That'd be rude.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:54.080
Then call us "sirs," and not "guys."

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.450
My bad.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.080
That too. You mean, "Forgive me."

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.700
Yes... Forgive me.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.540
Stop that, Ganba.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.250
He'd be on the team if he
 had the superhuman surgery too.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.410
But now, he's just a test jumper.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.790
He merely checks
 the ramp and weather condition.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.830
Why refuse the surgery?

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.160
If you were a superhuman,
 you could've won gold.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.660
You guys...

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.120
I mean, you sirs can't win a medal?

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.160
What did you say?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.500
Don't. What if the media sees you?

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.780
Drop the attitude.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.160
Ganba!

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:36.870
What's that?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.790
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.940
This world that you couldn't forgive
 is such a beautiful place

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.240
Are you saying everything that
 bears sadness is evil?

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:24.580
Even if the children crumble
 with guns of reality pointed at them

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.580
I am me and nothing else

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.580
I gain through gunpoint

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.750
Ready to fight

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.830
I'll rise like the break of dawn

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.290
I save them for the final day

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.370
Dream of the world
 for me and "fantasia"

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.370
It's time to go
 Unshaken mind

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.620
Change the world

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.950
I shake off my wavering gaze

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.910
And find my beloved justice

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:07.290
I live for the tomorrow
 that is unspoken of

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.080
Amidst evanescence and pain

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.700
Only the break of day drives me on

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.120
Until the day
 everything has returned

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.910
I face such horror tonight

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.970
(I Call Your Name
 in the Flowering City)

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.500
(January, the 47th of Shinka Era
 Sapporo)

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.160
I'm still woozy.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.700
Ghosts get sick on airplanes?

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.700
High up, the energy of
 Earth and humans is diluted.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.500
Is that how it works?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:42.700
Could be.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.870
Don't take Emi seriously.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.750
(Welcome to the Winter
 International Sports GP)

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.000
Sorry to bother you on New Year's.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.620
I'm Komparu of the Sports GP.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.620
Lively, isn't it?

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:01.160
The Sapporo International Sports GP.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.370
It shows that the riot 4 years ago
 is in the past.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.000
We must make it a success.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.390
All eyes are on the ski jump.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.370
They're really popular.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.890
The Three Birdmen.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.160
It's no longer the post-war era.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.950
We hopped at the 39th of Shinka Era
 Tokyo Sports GP.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:23.290
We stepped at the 45th of Shinka Era
 Osaka Expo.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:27.530
This time, we'll jump to finish off
 Japan's restoration.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.450
Win bronze, silver, and gold
 in the ski jump.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.410
That's the big shots' ideals...

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:37.120
But the three key men
 ended up like this.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.870
Lightning made flowers
 bloom on their heads.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.080
It's him. He did it.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.700
- Him?
 - Koichi Amato.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.370
The test jumper that was with us.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:01.290
Mr. Amato is a regular human.
 He couldn't do this.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.580
Who knows?

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.580
Maybe he came upon some weird power.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.410
It's common, right?

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.160
Right, Superhuman Bureau?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.580
Don't take it out on them.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.200
They're here to solve the problem.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.790
Then fix this.
 We can't jump like this.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.700
Is that true?

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:23.750
It doesn't affect
 their daily lives, but...

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.390
It doesn't bend,
 so we can't wear helmets.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.000
We're preparing helmets with holes.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.370
You idiot.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.330
You want us to compete
 looking like this?

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.770
It's humiliating.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:44.360
But Forest of Light Hill's
 opening ceremony is in 2 days.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.870
It'll be the premiere.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.830
The Three Birdmen will do
 an exhibition jump.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.370
The schedule is fixed.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.660
We need you to solve this by tomorrow.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:59.330
The Bureau protects superhumans.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.880
We don't do mysterious phenomena.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.830
The Sapporo GP is
 a huge national event.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:08.880
It's for Japan.
 I guess we can't be picky.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.290
What is it?

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.080
Look.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:15.620
That's it!

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.790
Those clouds attacked us.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.080
I'll go see.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:20.910
Meteortail!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.410
Everybody, run!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.540
A witch girl!

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.120
Meteortail!

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.910
They're too quick.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.790
Causing chaos again.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.180
And it's not helping either.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.200
Wake up, Hoshinoko.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:06.950
Thanks.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.330
Ow... You're pretty heavy.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:10.580
My head.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.410
There's no flower.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.500
Fuurouta!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:20.120
I'm so numb. I'm totally out of it.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.040
You're fine too?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.620
If you're both fine, that means...

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.700
Give me a lightning rod.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.380
- Hurry.
 - Yes.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.040
Meteortail!

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.750
Are you okay?

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.450
How rare for you to take risks.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:50.500
Once in a while.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:53.120
We need to find the cause quick,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.330
or Sapporo will be
 a human flower garden.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.290
You have a point.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.290
What the...

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.120
What did you do?

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.620
Are you Iwashita?

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.470
It's not Iwashita. It's Ganba.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.080
This flower is your doing, isn't it?

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:21.980
No clue.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:26.410
If we can't be in the GP,
 then you get a chance.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.230
Because humans can compete too.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.410
I haven't done anything.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:34.450
Don't lie. I saw you mutter something.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.410
I saw it.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.660
You know something. Say it.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:41.910
Or else...

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:47.120
See?

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.120
This is my power.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.330
A sports superhuman
 with a modified body.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:53.720
Stop it, Iwashita.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.790
It's not Iwashita, it's Ganba.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:58.950
I threw away my name
 and had my body toyed with.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.250
I'm an artificial superhuman.
 What you dread.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.080
I don't dread you.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:08.410
Then why compete in the GP as a human?

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:12.580
You said you were a test jumper
 but you registered too.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.450
The committee did.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.700
Enough.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.120
Don't!

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.580
What a joke, huh?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.290
All our efforts
 are ruined by this flower.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.750
- Was this your wish?
 - No!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.080
I don't know anything.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.620
Still playing dumb?

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.620
Three Birdmen Ganba.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.790
We think it's a childish name too.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.200
But it's all for the GP.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:45.660
For the gold medal.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.900
Or else the surgery was meaningless.

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.270
Listen. You guys...

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.950
It's not "you guys." It's "you sirs."

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:56.120
Stop!

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.330
- Stop!
 - Don't.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.040
Don't chase him.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.950
- But...
 - It's fine.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.460
Are you a cop?

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.340
No. I came to see you.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.370
Mr. Koichi Amato.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.160
You're not in the dorms?

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.200
I was born and bred in Sapporo.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.200
You really not behind everything?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.200
Don't be afraid.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:39.370
There is a Superhuman Bureau
 that secures unidentified superhumans.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.200
They try to make them
 work for the nation.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.870
I want to protect you from them.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:53.950
Only body mods like muscles
 and nerves are allowed in the GP.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.330
No mechanical parts.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:00.200
Though superhumans,
 inherent capabilities are crucial.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.290
They really pushed the surgery on me.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:06.180
When I kept refusing,
 they called me a traitor.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.950
I was taken off the team
 as an example.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:11.440
Why?

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.570
I was scared.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:20.870
What if I became a superhuman
 but couldn't win a medal?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.040
I couldn't bring myself
 to sign that paper.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.080
I wasn't prepared to jump
 while representing Japan.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:33.910
Don't worry.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.750
I wouldn't act for my country now.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.040
I've made a great mistake.

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:42.870
Forgive me.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.660
That's it?

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:51.000
If you have special powers,
 you have to solve this case.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.160
But if it wasn't you, then who?

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.910
I have an idea.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:05.410
What an innocent smile.
 It's embarrassing just to watch.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.200
A nice smile.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.790
I was in middle school.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:12.160
There was a shrine where
 Forest of Light Hill is.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.700
There was a ritual that was held
 every New Year.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.750
There was a target in the woods.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:24.750
Hit the mark, and the god would
 rejoice and promise a good harvest.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.430
It was an age-old tradition.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.700
Each year, a boy turning 15
 was chosen to shoot.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.350
That year, I was chosen.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:49.790
That's right. The Forest of Light was
 once the forest of the Piricappi god.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.700
Piricappi.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.910
It's cold. How far are we going?

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:00.300
Ask Miss Emi.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.660
But it's great.
 Feels like home for ghosts.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:09.200
Is the cause for
 flowering humans really here?

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:14.250
Well, this time, it's our side
 that's causing it, so...

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.870
Only humans get flowers.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:21.440
So Kikko-chan, Fuurouta, and I
 were okay.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.500
But the Three Birdmen are superhumans.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:29.040
Artificial superhumans.
 They still have human bodies.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.500
I don't get it.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.870
You'll see.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.700
See? Over there.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.950
That thing?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.080
It's the symbol of the forest's god.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:43.840
Jiro-san.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.090
You guys.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:51.540
Mr. Amato, the test jump is cancelled.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:54.500
Really?
 But tomorrow's the opening event.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:57.370
But with
 the Three Birdmen like that...

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:01.410
I will check the conditions every day
 no matter what.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.830
That's my job as a test jumper.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:10.280
I can't let you go to the hill.
 Mr. Ganba's orders.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.450
What?

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.500
What right does he have?

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.200
We obey the national team's wish.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.160
That's the committee's job.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:19.450
Komparu.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.420
Please understand, Mr. Amato.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.040
Why are you here, Hitoyoshi?

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.000
You're behind this too?

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.040
No.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.160
The Bureau can't handle this...

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.620
Mr. Jaguar, Miss Emi's acting strange.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:43.160
Emi.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:46.200
That's not Miss Emi.
 It's something greater.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:47.200
What?

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:48.750
It's a god.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.620
It's Piricappi.
 The forest's god possessed her.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:53.620
No way.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.660
Forest of Light Hill was
 developed where the god's woods were.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.830
The god's name is Piricappi.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.870
It's the language of past dwellers.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.380
It means "beautiful seeds."

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:09.330
Piricappi plants seeds,
 grows flowers, and makes forests.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.540
So the human flowering
 was by this god?

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.330
Huh?

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.030
Why attack Mr. Amato?

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.200
It's all his fault.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.160
He loves skiing. He'd never do that.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.910
But he's a test jumper.
 Not an athlete...

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.330
Enough!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:42.080
It's not like fighting will
 wilt this flower.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:46.410
What should we do?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.980
Emi!
 Let's go, Kikko.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:05.080
Okay. Meteortail!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.360
Wait for me.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:26.080
What's that?

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:30.330
Stop, this place is off-limits.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:33.040
Hey, stop them.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.790
They won't stop.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:37.890
You guys too?

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.500
What's going on?

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:54.780
What is this?

00:16:56.450 --> 00:17:00.000
It's using Emi's powers
 to double its own.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.700
We have to stop them.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:02.790
There's no use.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:06.290
This is all a god's doing.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.160
It's not something ghosts can handle.

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:10.420
But...

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.790
It's time for the celebration!

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:27.270
What the...

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:30.250
The people turned into a forest.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:34.780
Turn them back!

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.830
- Stop!
 - Out of my way.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.200
Attacking Emi?

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.550
No, I'm bringing her back.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:54.420
So he does like her...

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:59.750
The GP comes first.
 The nation's dignity is at stake.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.890
Turning a blind eye?
 How Bureau-like.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.850
Only care about
 using superhumans for the country?

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.620
Ditch your childish ideals.

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:13.360
You don't even try to understand.

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.070
Stop it already!

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:18.250
I don't care about
 gods or superhumans.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.410
The country and government too.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.450
The athletes worked hard.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:27.290
They trained four years for the GP.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.960
If you're all so powerful,

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:33.250
stop quarrelling and fix everything.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.220
Put the ramp back to normal.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:40.470
Don't waste the four years
 of the athletes.

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:51.080
What?

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.620
But tomorrow's the opening event.

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:01.000
There was a ritual that was held
 every New Year.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.370
I see now.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.250
- Where to?
 - Move.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.330
Mr. Amato.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.290
I remember now.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.910
Today's the day of the ritual.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:12.420
You're jumping under these conditions?

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:14.540
- Yeah.
 - Impossible.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:17.800
Move. Shut up and watch.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:21.080
Mr. Amato.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:30.830
That's right.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:35.200
It'd be too lonely for the gods
 if it were just for humans.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.540
Is he going to jump through that gap?

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:43.870
He's not a superhuman.
 It's too far for a human.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.080
Tighten it.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.120
Tighten it.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:53.750
Release!

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.370
Move the forest, Kikko.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.040
It's impossible for a human.
 He'll crash.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.790
- Okay.
 - Don't!

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.330
He won't make it.

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.540
Don't interfere with the ritual.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.210
Well? It's a bull's-eye, Piricappi.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:36.200
Just like that day!

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:48.830
This is god's blessing?

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.350
Mr. Komparu.

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:53.910
Are you okay?

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.100
Huh? What happened?

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.580
Are you okay, Emi?

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.580
Yes... Where's Jiro?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:05.080
He's gone.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.330
Umm...

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.540
Forgive us.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.370
I was full of myself
 and acted horribly.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:22.410
We heard you risked yourself
 to cure us.

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:24.200
Thank you.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:25.630
You really are great.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.640
You guys... I mean, you sirs...

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:32.080
No, please call us "you guys."

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:37.410
I didn't have the courage
 to represent Japan.

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:41.530
So I wanted to at least
 do my job as a test jumper.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:43.580
That's all.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:45.830
Get those medals.

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:48.280
Forget superhumans and humans.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:50.500
You're athletes.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.670
Sorry for the trouble that time.

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:58.950
It was unlike you.

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:03.950
Old forgotten gods are like us Yokai.

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:05.670
We kind of clicked.

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:08.680
But it's all good.
 They won medals too.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:10.870
I suppose. But...

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:15.080
If the GP were to be held
 in Tokyo again,

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:16.810
what will happen?

00:22:17.660 --> 00:22:21.560
The old gods that sleep here
 can be trouble.

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:40.950
In this age where
 ideals are just a fantasy

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:47.950
Where are you going to
 reach out to?

00:22:48.250 --> 00:22:50.790
Alone by yourself

00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:52.620
Always

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:54.580
Always

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:57.060
With somebody's justice

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:05.500
You're suffering to protect what?

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:10.120
If you're still captured...

00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:11.950
I can't hold you

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.950
On these streets without any signs...

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:19.950
A child is crying

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:27.160
Ideals are just a toy, anyway

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:34.620
But you still reach out your hands

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:42.120
Righteous heroes are probably
 just beyond your reach

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:48.620
I don't mind
 I just want to keep watching...

00:23:49.580 --> 00:23:53.120
Just that one person

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:58.950
Ra-ri-re-ro ra-re-ri-ro ro-ro-ron-pa.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.160
I'm Devilo, my sister is Devila.

00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:03.500
De-ro-ron de-ro-ron de-de-de-no-de.

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:05.920
Gods are ugly, devils are beautiful.

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:08.250
It can't be known, sha-la-la-la-lan.

00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:10.870
I'm tearing up, an-do-ro-ro!
